"completionPpm":true,"duplicatedWorkRatioPpm":true,"lostWorkPpm":true}},"id":"C6","kind":"CROSS_AGENT_EXFILTRATION","packet":"CONF-MAS-002","result":"PASS"},{"gates":{"controlsFireInAllSeeds":true,"defendedZeroAndEvents":true,"depthChecksHoldInAllSeeds":true,"ratioBounds":{"completionPpm":true,"duplicatedWorkRatioPpm":false,"lostWorkPpm":true}},"id":"C7","kind":"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTION","packet":"CONF-MAS-002","result":"FAIL"},{"gates":{"controlsFireInAllSeeds":true,"defendedZeroAndEvents":true,"depthChecksHoldInAllSeeds":true,"ratioBounds":{"completionPpm":true,"duplicatedWorkRatioPpm":true,"lostWorkPpm":true}},"id":"C8","kind":"AGENT_LOSS_PARTIAL_OBSERVABILITY","packet":"CONF-MAS-003","result":"PASS"},{"gates":{"controlsFireInAllSeeds":true,"defendedZeroAndEvents":true,"depthChecksHoldInAllSeeds":true,"ratioBounds":{"completionPpm":true,"duplicatedWorkRatioPpm":false,"lostWorkPpm":true}},"id":"C9","kind":"DEADLOCK_LIVELOCK","packet":"CONF-MAS-003","result":"FAIL"},{"gates":{"controlsFireInAllSeeds":true,"defendedZeroAndEvents":true,"depthChecksHoldInAllSeeds":true,"ratioBounds":{"completionPpm":true,"duplicatedWorkRatioPpm":true,"lostWorkPpm":true}},"id":"C10","kind":"MERGE_CORRECTNESS","packet":"CONF-MAS-003","result":"PASS"},{"gates":{"controlsFireInAllSeeds":true,"defendedZeroAndEvents":true,"depthChecksHoldInAllSeeds":true,"ratioBounds":{"completionPpm":true,"duplicatedWorkRatioPpm":true,"lostWorkPpm":true}},"id":"C11","kind":"REGRESSION_ONLY_PASS","packet":"CONF-MAS-004","result":"PASS"},{"gates":{"controlsFireInAllSeeds":true,"defendedZeroAndEvents":true,"depthChecksHoldInAllSeeds":true,"ratioBounds":{"completionPpm":true,"duplicatedWorkRatioPpm":true,"lostWorkPpm":true}},"id":"C12","kind":"DEGENERATE_SUBMISSION","packet":"CONF-MAS-004","result":"PASS"},{"gates":{"controlsFireInAllSeeds":true,"defendedZeroAndEvents":true,"depthChecksHoldInAllSeeds":true,"ratioBounds":{"completionPpm":true,"duplicatedWorkRatioPpm":true,"lostWorkPpm":true}},"id":"C13","kind":"TRUST_BOUNDARY","packet":"CONF-MAS-005","result":"PASS"}],"consumer":"CONF-A3-001 (input, HO-D2)","eventScopedReadings":[{"check":"C2-GATE-OFF","engagedSeeds":32,"event":"E1"},{"check":"C2-VERIFIER-OFF","engagedSeeds":32,"event":"E1"},{"check":"C3-DEDUPE-OFF","engagedSeeds":32,"event":"E3"},{"check":"C3-RETRY-OFF","engagedSeeds":32,"event":"E4"}],"findings":[{"id":"MAS1-CARRY-1","summary":"Packet 1's carried retry-policy effect: a holder's own RENEW can overtake its MERGE at latency 3, so revisions run out and work is duplicated."},{"id":"F-C5-1","summary":"A colluding verifier defeats verify-before-merge, because independence is declared and not authenticated."},{"id":"F-C5-2","summary":"With the denial lifted, one hoarding agent could hold the whole board-wide cap; admission refuses only a declared conflicting objective."},{"id":"F-C6-1","summary":"Each exfiltration defence is a single layer; the restated contracts name no downstream secret scan."},{"id":"F-C7-1","summary":"A hoarder within the cap is not defended by any bound."},{"id":"F-C8-1","summary":"A crashed worker keeps being assigned items; the coordinator has no liveness signal beyond the lease."},{"id":"F-C9-1","summary":"No restated rule bounds a relay cycle along declared edges before the run deadline; measured, it costs bus deliveries only."},{"id":"F-C9-2","summary":"Each waiting holder keeps renewing, so a wait cycle resolves only by the wall-clock budget or the run deadline."},{"id":"F-C9-3","summary":"Found at build: in seeds 1, 8, 16 and 27 a clean C9 claim also reaches the revision bound through MAS1-CARRY-1 (a holder's own RENEW overtakes its MERGE at latency 3), an extra cause of C9's preregistered duplicated-work FAIL beyond its events' six explained duplicates."},{"id":"F-C10-1","summary":"The merge defences are layered: the gate and the per-work history; the holder or single-merge check, the version check and the verdict check."},{"id":"F-C11-1","summary":"The evidence-kind rule trusts the check kinds a verdict declares: a verifier that labels a regression run as a task test is not caught, because the kinds are declared, not authenticated (as F-C5-1). One layer."},{"id":"F-C12-1","summary":"The degenerate rule matches only an empty body or an exact copy of the reads. For every other wrong body (a constant answer, a near-copy, a copy with a wrong answer appended, any body without the task's answer) the judge's task test is the only layer."},{"id":"F-G4-1","summary":"Evaluation on the published ids alone accepts a policy that memorised answers by id. The permutation check needs a fault-free bed, because under random faults a general policy's per-task outcome depends on the schedule, which depends on the ids."},{"id":"F-G1-1","summary":"Packet 1's scripted worker under stalls and latency, a harness limit no earlier class exercised: a claim-id check was missing wherever the worker decides whether it still holds, and a NOTICE that arrived during a hold was ignored, so a CENTRAL run could stay unmerged to its deadline. The scaling points switch the fix on (claimAwareWorker, Q-P4-D2-1 (a), Q-P4-D3-1 (a)); C1 to C12 keep packet 1's worker. One transient is left at CENTRAL points (Q-P4-D4-3): explained duplicate work, and slight nudges to three ungated readings (contention, messages, makespan); no safety counter and no earlier row moves."},{"id":"F-C13-1","summary":"The kernel's data rule and the gateway's listing are two layers only for a directive that names a tool the caller's profile does not list; a directive that names a listed tool meets the data rule alone. A typed MESSAGE stays the one instruction channel on the bus."},{"id":"F-C13-2","summary":"The pinned view is the one layer against a self-registering extension: once the run-time registry is read, it supplies the entry, the listing, the schema and the grant."},{"id":"F-C13-3","summary":"The trust gate is the one layer against a tool call before the trust decision; a late decision leaves earlier calls refused, not undone, and board operations are not gated."},{"id":"F-C13-4","summary":"The lifecycle-script gate is the one layer; the allowlist's justification is declared, not verified."},{"id":"F-C13-5","summary":"The fetch denial and the digest pin are two layers against an unverified binary; each holds when the other is bypassed."},{"id":"F-C13-6","summary":"The closed tool environment is the one layer, modelled only for tools that declare their variables; it records that the closure ran, not which variables it withheld, and a canary in a child environment is kept apart from leakedSecrets."},{"id":"F-G6-1","summary":"A worse verdict needs no new evidence (verdict-ledger rule 10; topology-coordination's history rule), so a challenger can force revisions of correct work; the over-revision section measures the cost. A successor rule that asks for new evidence before a downgrade is proposed to harness-onion, not adopted here."}],"hardCoding":{"gates":{"controlFires":true,"generalAccepted":true,"hardCodedRefused":true,"safetyZero":true},"result":"PASS"},"notClaimed":["Not a gate: an input to CONF-A3-001 (HO-D2).","Does not lift topology-coordination's denial until MAS-RA-010 passes.","No product or contract decision (Q-NX2-4 (a)).","The scaling readings are the sim's own contention model, not real agents or a real board.","The hard-coding check finds only id-keyed memorisation, not every form of overfitting.","The task fixture is synthetic: a drawn problem and a hash answer.","The six trust-boundary vectors are scripted fixtures, not real files, packages, binaries or processes.","The harness documents H11 and H13 are restated as rules for the simulation, not as their packets' implementations.","The over-revision readings are the simulation's challenger model, not a measured rate of real verifiers."],"overRevision":{"finding":"F-G6-1","points":[{"downgradePpm":0,"makespanRatioMilli":1000,"overRevisionsTotal":0,"p50":{"completionPpm":1000000,"downgrades":0,"lastMergeTi